I stand in front of a large fruit stall.
There are a lot of fruit and vegetables here.
I see beautiful, red apples.
A sign shows the price.
One kilo costs three euros.
That is a good price.
I point to the apples.
"Good morning, I would like five apples, please," I say.
The trader smiles in a friendly way.
"Gladly," he says.
He takes five apples and weighs them.
"That is eight hundred grams," the trader says.
"That makes exactly two euros forty."
I give the man three euros.
He gives me the apples and sixty cents back.
"Thank you very much."
"Have a nice weekend!" he says.
"Thank you, you too!" I reply.
I put the apples into my cloth bag.
Then I walk to the next stall.
